#DESCRIPTION
Absorbing-particle boundary-condition test (pure particle push).

Electromagnetic field solver is turned OFF (solveEM=F, useHybridPIC=F), so the
fields stay frozen at the uniform initial state and the run reduces to the
particle pusher.  This isolates the ABSORBING particle boundary condition: a
single kinetic ion species (q=+1, m=1) is initialised with a bulk flow toward
the +x face (ux > 0), and BOTH x faces are ABSORBING particle boundaries (a
particle crossing a face is removed and tallied).

Using `absorb` on both x faces means NO face re-injects particles (a reflecting
face would re-inject and hide the absorption), so as the run proceeds the ions
drain out through the x faces and the particle kinetic energy (Epart) DECAYS
toward zero -- the opposite of the reflecting-wall test, where specular
reflection conserves Epart.  y and z are thin (fake-2D/1D) and periodic.  The
magnetic field is zero so the ions move ballistically (no gyro-trap).

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-3.2                    xMin  [code units; Lx = 6.4 d_i]
 3.2                    xMax
-0.05                   yMin
 0.05                   yMax
-0.05                   zMin
 0.05                   zMax

#NCELL
8                       nCellX
1                       nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
16                      maxBlockSizeX
1                       maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
F                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

#PARTICLEBOXBOUNDARY
0                       iSpecies
absorb                  particleBoxBoundaryLo  (x; absorb + tally on exit)
absorb                  particleBoxBoundaryHi  (x; absorb + tally on exit)
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryLo  (y)
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryHi
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryLo  (z)
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryHi

#RESAMPLING
F                       doReSampling    (off: split/merge would regenerate particles
                                        and mask the draining / keep rho non-zero)

Electromagnetic field solver OFF: the fields are frozen at the uniform initial
state and the run exercises only the particle pusher + boundary absorption.
#SOLVEEM
F                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
F                       useHybridPIC

Single kinetic ion species (q = m = 1).
#PLASMA
1                       nSpecies
1.0                     mass
1.0                     charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
5.0                     rho [amu/cc]   Species 0: ions
40.0                    ux [km/s]      bulk flow toward +x absorbing wall
0.5                     uy [km/s]      small oblique component
0.0                     uz [km/s]
0.0                     T [K]
0.0                     bx [T]         zero B: particles stream ballistically
0.0                     by [T]         (a guide field would gyrate the ions and
0.0                     bz [T]         trap them, blocking wall crossing)
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.02                    dt

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI   [m]
1.0e5                   uNormSI   [m/s]

#MONITOR
200                     dnReport

#SAVELOG
1                       dnSavePic
1                       dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
100                     npcelx
1                       npcely
1                       npcelz

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 var ascii planet    plotString
-1                      dn
10.0                    dt
1                       dx
rhoS0 uxS0 uyS0 uzS0 Bx By Bz Ex Ey Ez   plotVar

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
20.0                    TimeMax

#RUN
